Elif needs a short break.
I go to the till.
This is my first shift in the café.
But I have already learned to operate the till correctly.
An older gentleman comes to the counter.
"Good morning," I say.
"Good morning."
"I would like a black coffee and a Brötchen, please," he says.
"With pleasure," I answer.
I take a small paper bag.
Carefully, I bag the Brötchen.
Then I type in the order.
"That is four Euro and fifty cents, please," I say.
The gentleman gives me a five-Euro note.
I give him fifty cents back.
"Would you like the receipt?" I ask.
"No, thank you," he answers.
He takes his coffee and the Brötchen.
"Have a nice Saturday," the gentleman says.
"Thank you, you too!" I call.
It is a good feeling to help out here.
